# A hostile PDF's scripts in the viewer (pdf-scripts-hostile.pdf is
# forms-js-hostile.pdf of tools/pdf-make-form-tests.py): its document
# script finds no page, network, storage or timers of the page, and the
# escape through Function's constructor finds only its own realm; a
# button whose script never ends is stopped by the time limit while the
# viewer goes on answering (the zoom changes meanwhile), and the realm
# answers the next button; a button that takes memory without end ends
# the document's scripts and nothing else. The page is 400 x 200 at zoom
# 1.25: a point (x, y) of it is at (200 + 1.25 x, 142 + 1.25 (200 - y)).
resize 900 700
open pdf-scripts-hostile.pdf
advance 600 8
assert-value field-10-0 fetch!ReferenceError;XMLHttpRequest!ReferenceError;document!ReferenceError;window!ReferenceError;escape=undefined;setTimeout!ReferenceError;localStorage!ReferenceError;launchURL=undefined
assert-value zoom auto
click 287 248
key ctrl+=
advance 100 2
assert-value zoom 1.5
key ctrl+-
advance 100 2
assert-value zoom 1.25
advance 1500 10
assert-console ran too long and was stopped
click 437 248
advance 400 5
assert-value field-10-0 alive
# The memory bomb: the document's scripts end, the viewer does not.
click 587 248
advance 1500 10
assert-console used too much memory and were stopped
key ctrl+=
advance 100 2
assert-value zoom 1.5
